# Workload plugins compiled into the daemon, as Go build tags.
#
# THIS FILE IS AN INTERFACE. Downstream packaging reads it to decide
# what to pass to `go build -tags`; build/build.sh reads it for the same
# purpose. Before it existed, the list was hardcoded in build.sh and
# duplicated by hand downstream, which meant adding a plugin here
# silently produced a package without it: no error, no warning, just a
# probe that never appears. A comment saying "keep these in sync" is
# not a control.
#
# Format, so it stays trivially parseable from make, sh, and Go:
#   - one tag per line
#   - blank lines and #-comments ignored
#   - no quoting, no continuation, no ordering significance
#
# Consumers should join the lines with commas. `make` users:
#   TAGS := $(shell grep -v '^\s*\#' build/workload-tags | tr '\n' ',' | sed 's/,$$//')
#
# Adding or removing a line changes what the shipped binary can probe.
# Treat it as a release-note item, not an implementation detail — a
# downstream build has no way to notice a NEW tag on its own.
#
# REQ 4.9 and design §9: plugins are compile-time only. There is no
# runtime loading, so this list is the whole story.

wl_wireguard
wl_postfix
wl_dovecot
wl_nginx_apache
